{"text": "theoretical", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">theorothycall</i>, probably from Latin <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">the\u014dr\u0113ticus</i> + <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">-al</i>, from Ancient Greek <i class=\"Polyt mention\" lang=\"grc\">\u03b8\u03b5\u03c9\u03c1\u03b7\u03c4\u03b9\u03ba\u03cc\u03c2</i> (the\u014dr\u0113tik\u00f3s).\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Adjective", "definitions": [{"definition": "Of or relating to theory; abstract; not empirical.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {"Antonym": ["practical"]}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["General Australian", "/\u02cc\u03b8i\u02d0\u02c8\u0279et.\u026a.k\u0259l/"], ["US", "/\u02cc\u03b8i.\u0259\u02c8\u0279\u025bt.\u026a.k\u0259l/"], ["UK", "/\u02cc\u03b8\u026a\u0259\u02c8\u0279\u025bt\u026ak\u0259l/"]]}